  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEE-Clean Cooking: Mid-term Evaluation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the assignment is to review, at mid-term, the progress made by the SEE-Clean Cooking programme, using the OECD-DAC criteria relevance, coherence, effectiveness, efficiency, and (likely) impact and sustainability.The Mid-term Review (MTR) generates evidence-based conclusions on past and ongoing activities, draws lessons learned and provides strategic recommendations for the remaining implementation period of the programme, and for potential future or follow-up interventions. Country cases studies for Cambodia and Uganda were developed, along with an overarching programme level report.The assignment was implemented by Transition International.</narrative>
  </description>
